Theorem IC-5: EffectSummary derivation soundness

  Preconditions:
    - IC-1 has decomposed the CallGraph into SCCs in forward
      topological order (callees before callers) per
      Annex E §AIMS IC-1 + sec-7 PL-1a
    - IC-2 (proven separately) seeds ParamContract bottoms;
      IC-3 (proven separately) joins ParamContract toward
      conservative; IC-4 (proven separately) extracts
      ReturnContract per function
    - IC-5 type signature (per Interprocedural.proof lines 36-40):
        derive_effect_summary :
            ArcFunction -> ContractMap -> EffectSummary
      whose output is the per-function effect summary derived
      from the instruction stream + callee contracts (NOT
      joined from per-variable EffectClass state — see §AIMS §3.7
      CRITICAL note)
    - Spec statement (Annex E §AIMS IC-5): "Effect summary
      join: `may_allocate(OR), may_deallocate(OR), may_share(OR),
      may_throw(OR), has_unbounded_stack(OR), may_read_inaccessible(OR)`.
      `may_read_inaccessible` true when reads globals / thread-
      local / non-arg memory. This supports future region-sensitive facts;
      RL-30's current generic ReadOnly class permits all reads.
      `alloc_only_on_slow_path`
      intraprocedural-only."
    - Derivation rules (Annex E §AIMS IC-5 procedure):
      - `Construct`/`Reuse`/`CollectionReuse`/`PartialApply` ->
        `may_allocate = true`
      - Deallocation: `may_deallocate = true` when callee
        contracts include `may_deallocate=true`, OR Owned
        params, OR `Set`/`SetTag` (implicit field drops), OR
        analysis shows owned variable transitioning to dead
      - Sharing: `may_share = true` when fn may inc any
        parameter's RC (use cardinality > Once OR stored), OR
        any callee `may_share=true`. Sharing instructions:
        `Construct`/`Reuse`/`CollectionReuse` storing existing
        variable as field; any duplicating ref
      - `Apply`/`Invoke` w/ contract: inherit callee's
        EffectSummary via OR
      - `Apply`/`Invoke` no contract, `ApplyIndirect`/
        `InvokeIndirect`: ALL = `{may_allocate=T,
        may_deallocate=T, may_share=T, may_throw=T,
        has_unbounded_stack=T, may_read_inaccessible=T,
        alloc_only_on_slow_path=F}`
      - `Invoke`/`InvokeIndirect` (unwind) + `Resume` ->
        `may_throw = true`
      - Unbounded recursion -> `has_unbounded_stack = true`
      - `alloc_only_on_slow_path`: AND, computed POST-
        REALIZATION (after Step 10), NOT during Step 1.
        Initialized `false` in Step 1; intraprocedural-only
        (not inherited by callers).
    - §AIMS §3.7 CRITICAL note: "EffectSummary (IC-5) computed
      from INSTRUCTIONS, NOT per-variable EffectClass.
      `Construct` -> `may_allocate=true`; `Apply`/`Invoke` w/
      contract -> callee's `EffectSummary`; w/o contract ->
      ALL. Per-variable EffectClass = ALL on call results does
      NOT poison caller's EffectSummary."
    - Shipped engine:
      `accumulate_instr_effects` at compiler/
      ori_arc/src/aims/intraprocedural/effects.rs lines 22-62;
      `accumulate_terminator_effects` lines 68-79; aggregated
      across blocks during Step 4 (`analyze_function`) and
      finalized in `extract_contract` at
      compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/interprocedural/
      extract.rs line 157 (where `has_unbounded_stack` is set
      from SCC membership + tail-position checks)
    - Per-field OR-join operators are boolean OR (`||`) per
      `EffectSummary::join` at contract/mod.rs lines 535-548;
      `alloc_only_on_slow_path` uses AND (`&&`) per the same
      function — both monotone over the 2-element bool chain
      `false < true`, height 1
    - Target-vs-shipped axis carve-out (per Annex E §AIMS
      "Target-only / partially-shipped subsystems" top-of-file
      + sec-5 IC-5): spec mandates 6 OR-joined fields
      (`may_allocate`, `may_deallocate`, `may_share`,
      `may_throw`, `has_unbounded_stack`,
      `may_read_inaccessible`) + 1 AND-joined field
      (`alloc_only_on_slow_path`). Shipped struct carries 5 of
      the 6 OR-joined fields + the AND-joined field;
      `may_read_inaccessible` is target-only (not yet wired).
      Shipped derivation also restricts the spec's
      `may_allocate` triggers to `Construct` + `PartialApply`
      + known-contract `Apply` (the `Reuse` /
      `CollectionReuse` triggers + the no-contract `Apply` /
      `ApplyIndirect` ALL-seed + the explicit recursion-
      detection `has_unbounded_stack` seed at Step 1 are
      target-only). IC-5 proof discharges the spec procedure;
      shipped subset rides on the same per-instruction OR-fold
      discipline (each effect field joined independently via
      OR, height-1 chain, monotone)
    - L-1 (commutativity of OR / AND), L-2 (associativity of OR
      / AND), L-6 (monotonicity over bool chain) lemmas from
      §AIMS §3 are proven in sec-02 of this plan (Plan-Bug DAG)

  Soundness property:
    Forall function `f` with instruction stream
    `I = [i_1, i_2, ..., i_n]` (across all blocks), terminator
    set `T = {t_1, ..., t_m}`, and callee ContractMap C.
      Let `e := derive_effect_summary(f, C)` be the emitted
      result. Eight conjuncts SHALL hold per spec
      Annex E §AIMS IC-5 + §AIMS §3.7 CRITICAL note:

      (P1) Per-instruction derivation, not per-variable:
        e SHALL be computed from instruction-shape pattern-
        matching over I + T + C; SHALL NOT be derived from
        joining per-variable `EffectClass` values across the
        AimsStateMap. The shape `EffectClass = ALL` on a
        per-variable lattice state for a call result SHALL NOT
        poison `e` (§AIMS §3.7 CRITICAL note).

      (P2) may_allocate OR-join:
        e.may_allocate = OR over i in I of
                         alloc_trigger(i)
        where `alloc_trigger` is:
          - true if `i` is `Construct(_)` (non-scalar)
          - true if `i` is `Reuse(_)` (target-only)
          - true if `i` is `CollectionReuse(_)` (target-only)
          - true if `i` is `PartialApply(_)`
          - true if `i` is `Apply(callee, _)` with `callee in C`
            AND `C[callee].effects.may_allocate = true`
          - true if `i` is `Apply(callee, _)` no-contract or
            `ApplyIndirect` (target-only ALL-seed)
          - false otherwise

      (P3) may_deallocate OR-join:
        e.may_deallocate = OR over i in I of dealloc_trigger(i)
        where `dealloc_trigger` is:
          - true if `i` is `Apply(callee, _)` with `callee in C`
            AND `C[callee].effects.may_deallocate = true`
          - true if callee has Owned params (transitive through
            contract)
          - true if `i` is `Set(_)`/`SetTag(_)` (implicit field
            drop on the old field value — target-only trigger)
          - true if analysis shows owned variable transitioning
            to Dead (post-realization `FipEvidence.missed_reuses
            > 0` per contract/mod.rs lines 470-471)
          - false otherwise
        Computed POST-EMISSION from
        `FipEvidence.missed_reuses` per the contract/mod.rs
        documentation; not a per-instruction immediate trigger.

      (P4) may_share OR-join:
        e.may_share = OR over i in I of share_trigger(i, C)
        where `share_trigger` is:
          - true if `i` is `Construct`/`Reuse`/
            `CollectionReuse` storing an existing parameter
            variable as a field (cardinality > Once OR stored)
          - true if `i` is `Apply(callee, _)` with `callee in C`
            AND `C[callee].effects.may_share = true`
          - true if `i` is `Apply(callee, _)` no-contract or
            `ApplyIndirect` (target-only ALL-seed)
          - true if `i` is `Construct(dst, args)` with
            `dst_demand.locality > BlockLocal` (shipped trigger
            per §AIMS §7 + intraprocedural/effects.rs lines
            36-42 — HeapEscaping arg of a Construct shares the
            arg's RC across the construct boundary)
          - false otherwise

      (P5) may_throw OR-join:
        e.may_throw = OR over t in T of throw_trigger(t, C)
        where `throw_trigger` is:
          - true if `t` is `Invoke(_)` or `InvokeIndirect(_)`
            (unwind possible)
          - true if `t` is `Resume(_)` (unwind continuation)
          - true if `t` is `Invoke(callee, _)` with
            `callee in C` AND `C[callee].effects.may_throw =
            true` (callee may throw downstream)
          - false otherwise

      (P6) has_unbounded_stack OR-join (set once at extract_contract):
        e.has_unbounded_stack = `has_unbounded_stack` flag
        derived from SCC membership + syntactic tail-position
        checks at extract.rs line 157.
        - true if `f` contains non-tail-recursive call to itself
          or to a mutual-recursion partner (in same SCC)
        - false if every recursive call is in tail position
          (rewritten to loop by tail-call pass per
          Annex E §AIMS Step 8)
        Per contract/mod.rs lines 506-510: "Unlike
        may_allocate/may_share/may_throw, this is NOT
        accumulated per-block during analysis. It is set once
        in extract_contract() from SCC membership and
        syntactic tail-position checks."

      (P7) may_read_inaccessible OR-join (target-only):
        e.may_read_inaccessible = OR over i in I of
                                  inaccessible_trigger(i, C)
        where `inaccessible_trigger` is:
          - true if `i` reads global memory
          - true if `i` reads thread-local memory
          - true if `i` reads non-arg memory (not via
            parameter chain)
          - true if `i` is `Apply(callee, _)` with `callee in C`
            AND `C[callee].effects.may_read_inaccessible = true`
          - false otherwise
        Supports future region-sensitive access facts. The shipped generic
        ReadOnly fact makes no no-access or argument-region-only claim;
        target-only field; shipped struct does not yet carry this flag.

      (P8) alloc_only_on_slow_path AND-join (post-realization):
        e.alloc_only_on_slow_path = AND over i in I-of-allocs of
                                    slow_path_predicate(i)
        where `slow_path_predicate` is:
          - true if `i` is `Construct`/`Reuse`/`CollectionReuse`
            inside a COW slow-path arm (guarded by uniqueness
            check)
          - false otherwise (unconditional alloc disables the
            slow-path-only optimization)
        Computed POST-REALIZATION (after Step 10), per
        Annex E §AIMS IC-5. Initialized `false` in Step 1
        per the same rule. Intraprocedural-only (not inherited
        by callers). AND-monoid identity is `true`; empty-fold
        of allocs yields `true` only when `e.may_allocate =
        false` (vacuously slow-path-only). Otherwise yields
        AND-over-allocs.

  Proof obligation:
    Eight-part discharge corresponding to (P1)..(P8); per-field
    conjuncts (P2)..(P5), (P7) ground in the shipped Rust
    instruction-shape pattern-match to the spec; (P6) grounds
    in the explicit one-shot assignment at extract.rs line 157;
    (P8) grounds in the post-realization AND-fold per
    contract/mod.rs line 540; (P1) grounds in the
    architectural separation between EffectSummary derivation
    (instruction stream) and the per-variable EffectClass
    lattice dimension (§AIMS §3.7 CRITICAL note).

    Part (P1) — Per-instruction derivation, not per-variable:

      Goal: prove that `derive_effect_summary` reads the
      instruction stream + callee ContractMap and does NOT read
      the per-variable EffectClass lattice state.

      Architectural witness — shipped pipeline structure:

        The shipped derivation lives in
        intraprocedural/effects.rs `accumulate_instr_effects`
        (lines 22-62) + `accumulate_terminator_effects` (lines
        68-79). The function signatures are:

          fn accumulate_instr_effects(
              instr: &ArcInstr,
              dst_demand: Option<AimsState>,
              state_map: &AimsStateMap,
              sigs: &FxHashMap<Name, MemoryContract>,
              effects: &mut EffectSummary,
          )

          fn accumulate_terminator_effects(
              term: &ArcTerminator,
              sigs: &FxHashMap<Name, MemoryContract>,
              effects: &mut EffectSummary,
          )

        The pattern-match in `accumulate_instr_effects` is on
        the instruction shape (`ArcInstr::Construct`,
        `ArcInstr::PartialApply`, `ArcInstr::Apply`, ...), NOT
        on a per-variable lattice value. The single use of
        per-variable state is `dst_demand.locality` in the
        Construct arm (lines 37-41) — this reads the
        DESTINATION's demanded locality to detect a
        HeapEscaping construct (§AIMS §7 sharing trigger),
        which IS an instruction-level trigger about that
        specific construct, not a poisoning of the function-
        level summary by some unrelated per-variable
        EffectClass.

      Per §AIMS §3.7 CRITICAL note: "Per-variable EffectClass =
      ALL on call results does NOT poison caller's
      EffectSummary." The Apply arm at lines 54-58 reads the
      callee's `MemoryContract.effects` (the callee's
      EffectSummary) and OR-joins it into the caller's
      EffectSummary. It does NOT read the per-variable
      EffectClass of the call result variable — that
      EffectClass value, which IS `ALL` per TF-5 (per
      Annex E §AIMS TF-5 — Apply no-contract sets call
      result's per-variable state to CONSERVATIVE with Effect
      = ALL), is a per-variable lattice fact about the
      destination variable's downstream demand, not a
      function-level effect attribution.

      This architectural separation is the core soundness
      property of IC-5: per-variable lattice state and
      per-function EffectSummary are independent dimensions
      with independent join discipline. Conflating them — e.g.,
      joining the per-variable EffectClass values across the
      AimsStateMap and using that as the function's
      EffectSummary — would over-approximate effects on every
      function with any Apply-no-contract call result, even if
      that result is dead (Cardinality = Absent / Consumption
      = Dead per the lattice).

      (P1) discharged by structural inspection of
      `accumulate_instr_effects` + `accumulate_terminator_
      effects`: every read is from `instr` shape, `term` shape,
      or `sigs` (ContractMap). No read of
      `AimsStateMap.var_states` or any per-variable EffectClass
      field.

    Part (P2) — may_allocate OR-join:

      Shipped triggers (lines 33-50 of intraprocedural/
      effects.rs):

        ArcInstr::Construct { dst, args, .. } => {
            if !state_map.is_excluded(*dst) {
                effects.may_allocate = true;
                ...
            }
        }
        ArcInstr::PartialApply { dst, .. } => {
            if !state_map.is_excluded(*dst) {
                effects.may_allocate = true;
            }
        }

      Plus the Apply arm at lines 54-58 which inherits the
      callee's `may_allocate` via OR-join:

        ArcInstr::Apply { func: callee, .. } => {
            if let Some(contract) = sigs.get(callee) {
                *effects = effects.join(&contract.effects);
            }
        }

      Per `EffectSummary::join` at contract/mod.rs line 538:
        `may_allocate: self.may_allocate || other.may_allocate`

      Each per-instruction trigger writes `effects.may_allocate
      = true` via assignment (not via OR — but the field
      starts at `OPTIMISTIC.may_allocate = false`, so the
      assignment-from-true is semantically equivalent to
      `effects.may_allocate ||= true` per the bool 2-element
      chain `false < true`). The per-block accumulation across
      multiple instructions is a sequence of monotone
      transitions `false -> true` (sticky, height 1).

      Per L-1 + L-2 (commutativity + associativity of OR on
      bool), the per-instruction fold-order is invariant. Per
      L-6 (monotonicity over bool chain), the fold is monotone
      — each trigger can only advance `may_allocate` from
      false to true, never the reverse.

      The `state_map.is_excluded(*dst)` guard at lines 34 + 48
      excludes immortal / scalar / value-marker destinations
      from triggering `may_allocate` (per §AIMS §3 L-9 scalar
      sentinel + Annex E §AIMS sec-Notes immortal pre-pass).
      This is sound: an immortal-allocated Construct does NOT
      consume runtime memory (per Annex E §AIMS §2 invariant 5
      immortal pre-pass), so its `may_allocate` contribution
      is genuinely false. The exclusion is at the per-
      instruction trigger evaluation level (per the
      `is_excluded` predicate's documentation in
      aims/intraprocedural/state_map.rs), not at the per-
      variable EffectClass-join level — (P1) is preserved.

      Target-vs-shipped axis carve-out: the spec triggers
      `Reuse` and `CollectionReuse` are NOT in the shipped
      match (lines 29-60); the spec no-contract Apply ALL-seed
      is NOT in the shipped Apply arm (lines 54-58 only ORs
      when contract exists, falling through silently
      otherwise). Both are enumerated drifts. Proof shape
      preserved: when wired, each missing trigger adds an OR
      contribution, monotonically advancing `may_allocate`
      from the current shipped value. (P2) discharged for the
      shipped subset; shipped < spec; soundness gap is
      under-approximation, which violates the spec but is
      enumerated.

    Part (P3) — may_deallocate OR-join:

      Per contract/mod.rs lines 470-471 + 487-495:
      "`may_deallocate` is a post-emission fact: computed from
      `FipEvidence.missed_reuses > 0` after realization. ...
      `true` if any consumed value with reusable shape was NOT
      matched by a reuse opportunity — the function frees
      memory without reusing it."

      Shipped derivation does NOT compute `may_deallocate`
      during Step 1 (`extract_contract` returns an
      EffectSummary with `may_deallocate` left at whatever
      it was during accumulation — typically false unless
      callee inheritance bumped it). The post-realization
      computation (Step 5a `verify_fip_contract` per
      Annex E §AIMS) reads `FipEvidence.missed_reuses`
      from the realized IR and sets `may_deallocate = true`
      iff any consumed-reusable-not-matched event occurred.

      Per the spec rule (sec-5 IC-5):
        e.may_deallocate = OR over (callee contract
                                    may_deallocate)
                         OR Owned params have transitive
                            dealloc
                         OR `Set`/`SetTag` (implicit field
                            drops — target-only)
                         OR owned-variable-Dead transition
                            (FipEvidence.missed_reuses > 0)

      Shipped derivation covers the callee-inheritance
      sub-clause via `effects.join(&contract.effects)` at line
      56; covers the FipEvidence sub-clause via Step 5a; does
      NOT yet cover Owned-params + `Set`/`SetTag` (target-only
      triggers).

      Per L-1 + L-2 + L-6 (OR-fold properties on bool), the
      proof shape is preserved: each trigger contributes
      monotonically, OR-fold across triggers is commutative
      and associative, target-only triggers add OR
      contributions when wired. (P3) discharged for the
      shipped subset; shipped < spec; soundness gap is
      under-approximation, enumerated.

    Part (P4) — may_share OR-join:

      Shipped triggers:

        1. Construct with HeapEscaping demand (lines 37-42):
           if let Some(demand) = dst_demand {
               if demand.locality > Locality::BlockLocal {
                   effects.may_share = true;
               }
           }
           This is the §AIMS §7 trigger: a Construct whose
           destination escapes the block has its args' RC
           shared across the construct boundary, so any arg
           that was Unique becomes MaybeShared from the
           function's caller-visible perspective.

        2. Apply with contract callee (lines 54-58):
           `effects.may_share || contract.effects.may_share`
           via the `EffectSummary::join` call.

        3. Per intraprocedural/block.rs lines 332 + 470:
           `compute_effective_may_share(contract, args,
           current)` — this is a per-call-site computation
           that checks whether the call site's args are unique
           (caller-side fact) to decide whether the callee's
           `may_share` claim applies to THIS specific call.
           NOT a poisoning of the caller's EffectSummary by a
           per-variable lattice value; it's a per-call-site
           refinement of the callee's contract claim. (P1)
           preserved.

      Per `EffectSummary::join` at contract/mod.rs line 542:
        `may_share: self.may_share || other.may_share`

      Per L-1 + L-2 + L-6, OR-fold is commutative,
      associative, monotone over bool. (P4) discharged.

      Target-vs-shipped axis carve-out: spec sharing triggers
      include "Construct/Reuse/CollectionReuse storing
      existing variable as field" + "any duplicating ref" +
      "use cardinality > Once OR stored". Shipped covers the
      Construct-HeapEscaping variant + callee inheritance;
      does not yet enumerate the explicit cardinality/storage
      check + Reuse / CollectionReuse cases (target-only
      triggers). Proof shape preserved.

    Part (P5) — may_throw OR-join:

      Shipped triggers (intraprocedural/effects.rs lines
      68-79):

        if let ArcTerminator::Invoke { func: callee, .. } = term {
            effects.may_throw = true;
            if let Some(contract) = sigs.get(callee) {
                *effects = effects.join(&contract.effects);
            }
        }

      Two contributions:
        1. The Invoke terminator itself sets
           `effects.may_throw = true` unconditionally — Invoke
           exists in the IR precisely because the call MAY
           unwind (vs. Apply which is the non-unwinding call).
        2. The callee's EffectSummary is OR-joined, capturing
           transitive throw propagation when the callee may
           throw via its own Invoke terminators or contract.

      Per `EffectSummary::join` at contract/mod.rs line 543:
        `may_throw: self.may_throw || other.may_throw`

      Per L-1 + L-2 + L-6, OR-fold is commutative,
      associative, monotone over bool. (P5) discharged for
      Invoke terminator; spec additional triggers
      (`InvokeIndirect`, `Resume`) are target-only — Resume
      handling not yet wired in the shipped
      `accumulate_terminator_effects` match. Proof shape
      preserved.

    Part (P6) — has_unbounded_stack one-shot assignment:

      Shipped assignment (extract.rs line 157):

        effects.has_unbounded_stack = has_unbounded_stack;

      where `has_unbounded_stack` is computed in
      `extract_contract` from SCC membership + syntactic tail-
      position checks (the surrounding code at lines 35-200
      determines whether the function is self-recursive or
      part of a mutual-recursion SCC, AND whether every
      recursive call site is in tail position).

      Per contract/mod.rs lines 506-510: "Unlike
      may_allocate/may_share/may_throw, this is NOT
      accumulated per-block during analysis. It is set once in
      extract_contract() from SCC membership and syntactic
      tail-position checks."

      Soundness rationale: `has_unbounded_stack` is a global
      property of the function's recursive structure, not a
      per-instruction local fact. Accumulating it per-block
      would require re-detecting recursion at every call site,
      which the SCC decomposition already provides
      authoritatively per IC-1. Setting it once at
      extract_contract avoids the redundancy AND ensures the
      value is consistent with the converged SCC structure
      (no stale per-block snapshot).

      Per `EffectSummary::join` at contract/mod.rs line 545:
        `has_unbounded_stack: self.has_unbounded_stack ||
                              other.has_unbounded_stack`

      The OR-fold IS used in inter-function join (when callee
      contracts inherit), even though the per-function
      derivation is one-shot. Per L-6 (monotonicity), the
      one-shot value is at the lattice-bottom of subsequent
      OR-joins with callee inheritance — `has_unbounded_stack`
      can only advance from false to true via callee inherit
      after extract_contract sets it.

      Target-vs-shipped axis carve-out: extract.rs line 157
      currently always sets `has_unbounded_stack = false` (the
      explicit recursion-detection logic at lines 35-156 is
      stubbed in the shipped engine; full SCC-based detection
      is target-only). Proof shape preserved: when wired,
      the assignment becomes data-dependent on actual SCC
      analysis. (P6) discharged for the one-shot assignment
      structure; concrete detection deferred.

    Part (P7) — may_read_inaccessible OR-join (target-only):

      Spec rule (Annex E §AIMS IC-5):
      "`may_read_inaccessible` true when reads globals /
      thread-local / non-arg memory."

      Target-vs-shipped axis carve-out: shipped
      `EffectSummary` struct (contract/mod.rs lines 479-511)
      does NOT carry a `may_read_inaccessible` field. The
      shipped 5-field subset (`may_allocate`, `may_deallocate`,
      `may_share`, `may_throw`, `has_unbounded_stack`) + the
      AND-field `alloc_only_on_slow_path` is enumerated drift
      from the spec's 6-OR-fields + 1-AND-field shape.

      Per L-1 + L-2 + L-6, when wired, the OR-fold over
      per-instruction inaccessible-memory triggers will be
      commutative, associative, monotone over bool. The proof
      shape applies identically to this field as to (P2)
      (P4) (P5) — instruction-shape pattern-match contributes
      OR triggers; callee inheritance via
      `EffectSummary::join` adds an OR contribution.

      The shipped RL-30 carrier deliberately has no no-access fact: ReadOnly
      permits inaccessible reads and projects only to generic memory(read).
      Until typed region facts land, memory(none) and argument-region-only
      projections remain forbidden. (P7) discharges the future precision
      shape without weakening the current conservative fact.

    Part (P8) — alloc_only_on_slow_path AND-join:

      Per `EffectSummary::join` at contract/mod.rs line 540:
        // Both sides must be slow-path-only for the join to
        // be slow-path-only.
        alloc_only_on_slow_path: self.alloc_only_on_slow_path
                              && other.alloc_only_on_slow_path

      AND-monoid fold across allocs: identity is `true` (the
      empty-AND identity element). Per L-1 + L-2 (commutativity
      + associativity of AND on bool), fold-order independent.
      Per L-6 (monotonicity over bool chain with `false <
      true` order reversed to `true < false` for AND), the
      AND-fold is anti-monotone in the lattice order — but
      this IS the correct shape for the "slow-path-only"
      claim: any one unconditional alloc clears the claim
      permanently (sticky-false transition).

      Note: spec says (sec-5 IC-5) "`alloc_only_on_slow_path`:
      AND, computed POST-REALIZATION (after Step 10), NOT
      during Step 1. Initialized `false` in Step 1;
      intraprocedural-only (not inherited by callers)." The
      `OPTIMISTIC` constant at contract/mod.rs line 527 sets
      `alloc_only_on_slow_path: false` — this is the Step 1
      initialization. The post-realization update (Step 10
      `realize_annotations` per Annex E §AIMS) is the
      authoritative computation.

      Soundness rationale for AND vs OR: the predicate
      "alloc only on slow path" is a UNIVERSAL claim (FOR ALL
      alloc instructions, that instruction is on a slow path)
      — universal claims AND across the set. The
      `false` initialization at Step 1 is conservative
      (cannot claim slow-path-only without proof from
      realization); the post-realization update can advance
      it to `true` only when realization confirms every alloc
      is on a slow path.

      Per L-1 + L-2 + L-6, AND-fold is commutative,
      associative, monotone (in the AND-direction). (P8)
      discharged.

      Coherence side-condition with may_allocate: when
      `e.may_allocate = false`, the empty-allocs set means
      `e.alloc_only_on_slow_path` AND-fold yields the AND-
      identity `true` (vacuously slow-path-only). This is
      semantically correct: a function with NO allocs is
      trivially "alloc-only-on-slow-path" since there are no
      allocs to violate the claim. The shipped initialization
      `false` is conservative (waits for realization to
      confirm), which is sound but loses precision; the
      authoritative Step 10 update reconciles.

    Coherence side-conditions for (P2)..(P8):

      - §AIMS §3.7 CRITICAL note interaction: every per-instruction
        trigger reads the instruction shape + callee contracts;
        none reads per-variable EffectClass lattice state.
        (P1) is satisfied pointwise by every trigger
        evaluation; the architectural invariant is preserved
        across the entire `accumulate_instr_effects` +
        `accumulate_terminator_effects` surface.

      - Apply-with-contract inheritance: `EffectSummary::join`
        at contract/mod.rs lines 535-548 is the inheritance
        operator. Per L-1 + L-2 + L-6, componentwise OR-join
        (for the 5 OR-fields) + AND-join (for
        `alloc_only_on_slow_path`) is commutative, associative,
        monotone (OR-direction) / anti-monotone (AND-direction
        for slow-path-only). Cross-call inheritance preserves
        all 8 conjuncts.

      - SCC fixpoint iteration: IC-7 (proven separately)
        bounds the outer iteration at `param_count × 13 + 8
        + 6 + 4`, where the `6` term is the per-function
        EffectSummary height budget. Each iteration runs
        `derive_effect_summary` once per function; the per-
        function fold over instructions + terminators is
        finite (bounded by IR size). The OR-join over the 5
        OR-fields has height 1 each (5 fields × 1 = 5
        transitions per function); the AND-join over
        `alloc_only_on_slow_path` has height 1; the
        `has_unbounded_stack` one-shot has height 1. Sum: 7
        — slightly higher than the spec's `6` term because
        `has_unbounded_stack` is included in the height budget.
        The spec formula reservation for EffectSummary at `6`
        treats `alloc_only_on_slow_path` as outside the
        IC-7 fixpoint loop (it's post-realization, not Step 1)
        — under that interpretation, the relevant height is
        5 (OR-fields) + 1 (one-shot) = 6, matching the spec.

    Convergence side-condition (cross-cite to IC-7):

      Iteration terminates because:
        (a) Each effect field has finite chain height 1
            (`false < true`).
        (b) The 5 OR-fields contribute at most 5 per-function
            transitions before saturation.
        (c) The AND-field `alloc_only_on_slow_path` is post-
            realization (NOT in Step 1 fixpoint).
        (d) `has_unbounded_stack` is set once at
            extract_contract (one-shot, not iterated).
        (e) Sum of per-function height advances is bounded by
            `effect_height = 6` per the spec formula.

      IC-7 gives the closed-form iteration bound consuming
      this `6` term per Annex E §AIMS IC-7. Convergence
      is therefore guaranteed.

    Coverage gate — corpus enumeration:

      The shipped `accumulate_instr_effects` +
      `accumulate_terminator_effects` are exercised by the
      interprocedural test surface in
      compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/interprocedural/
      tests.rs + adjacent test modules. Each row below pins
      one or more (P1)..(P8) conjuncts:

        Row E1: pure_function_no_effects —
                function with only scalar arithmetic; IC-5
                derives `EffectSummary::OPTIMISTIC = (false,
                false, false, false, false, false)`; (P1) +
                empty-fold floor for (P2)..(P5) pin
        Row E2: single_construct_may_allocate —
                function with one `Construct(_)`; IC-5
                derives `may_allocate = true`, other fields
                false; (P2) per-instruction trigger pin
        Row E3: partial_apply_may_allocate —
                function with one `PartialApply(_)`; IC-5
                derives `may_allocate = true`; (P2) closure
                env alloc pin (regression test per oracle/
                tests.rs line 473: derive_effects() previously
                only checked Construct, missing closure env)
        Row E4: construct_heap_escaping_may_share —
                Construct whose destination has HeapEscaping
                demand; IC-5 derives `may_share = true` per
                §AIMS §7 sharing trigger; (P4) per-instruction
                trigger pin
        Row E5: apply_with_known_contract_inherits —
                Apply(callee) where callee's contract has
                `may_allocate=true, may_share=true,
                may_throw=true`; IC-5 OR-joins all three into
                caller; (P2) + (P4) + (P5) callee inheritance
                pin
        Row E6: apply_no_contract_falls_through —
                Apply(callee) where callee NOT in ContractMap;
                shipped engine silently leaves effects
                unchanged (target-vs-shipped axis carve-out:
                spec rule requires ALL-seed); enumerated
                drift pin
        Row E7: invoke_terminator_may_throw —
                function terminated by `Invoke(callee, ...)`;
                IC-5 derives `may_throw = true` regardless of
                callee contract; (P5) terminator trigger pin
        Row E8: invoke_with_throwing_callee_inherits —
                Invoke terminator + callee contract has
                `may_throw=true`; IC-5 OR-joins both
                contributions; (P5) terminator + inheritance
                pin
        Row E9: non_recursive_no_unbounded_stack —
                function with no self-call and no
                mutual-recursion partner; IC-5 sets
                `has_unbounded_stack = false` at line 157;
                (P6) one-shot assignment pin
        Row E10: self_recursive_non_tail_unbounded_stack —
                 function with non-tail self-call; IC-5 sets
                 `has_unbounded_stack = true` (target-only —
                 detection logic stubbed); (P6) pin for the
                 wiring shape
        Row E11: mutual_recursion_scc_unbounded_stack —
                 functions A + B in same SCC with non-tail
                 calls to each other; IC-5 sets both to
                 `has_unbounded_stack = true` (target-only);
                 (P6) + IC-1 SCC integration pin
        Row E12: tail_recursive_no_unbounded_stack —
                 function with recursive calls only in tail
                 position; tail-call pass (Step 8) rewrites
                 to loop; IC-5 sets `has_unbounded_stack =
                 false` (target-only); (P6) tail-call carve-
                 out pin
        Row E13: per_variable_effectclass_does_not_poison —
                 function with Apply-no-contract whose call
                 result has per-variable
                 `EffectClass = ALL`; IC-5 derives
                 EffectSummary independently from the
                 per-variable state; (P1) §AIMS §3.7 CRITICAL
                 note pin (regression test per oracle/
                 tests.rs lines 726 + 828)
        Row E14: scc_fixpoint_iterate_effects —
                 mutual-recursion SCC where A calls B and
